Package: gscalibrate
Type: Package
Title: Empirical Calibration for Per-Sample Gene Set Scores
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person('Joel', 'Minocha', role = c('aut','cre'),
                  email = 'you@example.com')
Description: Per-sample gene set scores (ssGSEA, GSVA, mean-z) are often entered
    as variables in regression models without any correction for inter-gene
    correlation, which inflates significance. This package computes empirical
    p-values against matched-random gene sets, reports the 95th-percentile null
    floor, and warns when the tested set is internally coherent enough that a
    draw-based null is unreliable. See Wu and Smyth (2012) <doi:10.1093/nar/gks461>
    for the correlation-aware alternative.
